     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is typically given as 850 mg three times daily or 1,000 mg twice daily. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day. This may be what the 1700 was meant to be, since 1700 is 2 \u00d7 850.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first. I can enter it with a note if you still want that."
      }
     ],
